  "summary": "Critic 4.1/10 again \u2014 first impression 4, world 4, legibility 5, automation 2, heat 7, night 2, onboarding 5, feel 4, coherence 5, keep-playing 3. Blind: OURS 0, EVEN 2 (information design, onboarding), THEIRS 8. The composition moved \u2014 onboarding and feel up, legibility and world down \u2014 but the total did not.",
  "biggest_gap": "THE CITY WILL NOT STAFF ITSELF, and one function is why. At tick 24000: 60 job capacity, 39 required slots, 41 employable workers \u2014 every required slot fillable twice over \u2014 yet twelve buildings are understaffed and eight have assigned:0, including five of seven coal generators and the only smelter. assign_jobs() at game/sim/citizens/citizen_job_board.gd:463 fills each site with while site.assigned < site.capacity and never reads site.required, a field it already has. The Hearth takes 8 against a requirement of 4 and everything built later starves. The blind judge names the same failure from the other end: a world-class anticipation layer bolted to nothing \u2014 make night 2 breach the wall, burn a housing block, kill four people the player can name.",
